<title>RUSSIA: Russia central bank sells 329 bln rbls bills.</title>
<headline>Russia central bank sells 329 bln rbls bills.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank sold 329.00 billion roubles ($56.7 million) nominal of GKO discount Treasury bills on behalf of the Finance Ministry on Tuesday, the bank's open-market operations department said.</p>
<p>The bank made the following transactions:</p>
<p>    Issue number			Nominal value</p>
<p>Sold:</p>
<p>    21076				   2.00 bln roubles</p>
<p>    21078				  49.00 bln roubles</p>
<p>    21079				 157.00 bln roubles</p>
<p>    21080				  37.00 bln roubles</p>
<p>    23007				  84.00 bln roubles</p>
<p>Total proceeds from the sales were 280.89 billion roubles.</p>
<p>Apart from intervening on its own account for liquidity-smoothing and monetary policy purposes, the central bank buys and sells securities as part of its management of the Finance Ministry's debt and asset portfolio.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
<p>($ = 5803 Russian Roubles)</p>
